   336	`C'^2 = nd > (n-1)(d-1) = 2 delta_aff = 2 r(C')` by Lemma 4.4, the inequality being
   337	`n + d - 1 > 0`. Hence `N = ker(pi_1(X' - C' u B_infty) -> pi_1(X' - B_infty))` is
   338	abelian. But `X' - B_infty = C^2` is simply connected, so `N` is all of
   339	`pi_1(X' - C' u B_infty) = pi_1(C^2 - D)`. Now use `(A)` of §1. `[]`
